  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "In acidic medium, $\\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{~S}$ is very feebly ionized giving very small concentration of sulphide ion for precipitation. Therefore, the most insoluble salts $\\mathrm{CuS}$ and $\\mathrm{HgS}$ are precipitated only.",
